---
import LessonPage from "../../../components/lesson/LessonPage.astro";
import { defineLesson } from "../../../data/lesson-schema.mjs";
export const page = defineLesson({
  "title": "Health & the body · A2 Vocabulary · Curriculum Map",
  "slug": "health-and-the-body",
  "level": "A2",
  "topic": "Health & the body",
  "category": "Vocabulary & Topics",
  "contentType": "vocabulary",
  "status": "ready",
  "description": "Name the parts of the body, describe how you feel, and handle a doctor’s visit. Learn the symptom chunks I have a headache , I have a sore throat , and I have a fever , say where i",
  "sequence": 13,
  "prerequisites": [],
  "related": [],
  "assessments": [
    "a2-exit"
  ]
});
---
<LessonPage page={page}>
<main class="wrap">
  <p class="kicker"><span class="dot"></span> Vocabulary · Lesson 13</p>
  <h1>Health &amp; <em>the body</em></h1>
  <p class="standfirst">Name the parts of the body, describe how you feel, and handle a doctor’s visit. Learn the symptom chunks <span class="ex">I have a headache</span>, <span class="ex">I have a sore throat</span>, and <span class="ex">I have a fever</span>, say where it hurts with <span class="ex">My back hurts</span>, and give simple advice with <span class="ex">You should rest</span>.</p>
  <div class="meta-row">
    <span class="tag">≈ 45–55 min</span>
    <span class="tag">body &amp; symptoms</span>
    <span class="tag">have · hurts · should</span>
    <span class="tag">11 interactive tasks</span>
  </div>

  <div class="lesson-flow" aria-label="Lesson flow">
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Notice</b><span>Read a short talk with a doctor.</span></div>
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Discover</b><span>have + symptom vs. body part + hurts.</span></div>
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Build</b><span>Choose, type, and build the chunks.</span></div>
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Use</b><span>Describe symptoms, give advice, call in sick.</span></div>
  </div>

  <p class="note-line">Two ways to talk about a problem: name the symptom with <span class="ex">have</span> (<span class="ex">I have a headache</span>) or name the body part with <span class="ex">hurts</span> (<span class="ex">My head hurts</span>). For advice, use <span class="ex">should</span> + base verb: <span class="ex">You should rest</span>.</p>

  <h2>Two-minute retrieval</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill>
    <h3>Three quick checks from earlier lessons</h3>
    <p class="choice-hint">Answer from memory, then check. Say each complete sentence aloud.</p>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Answer choices">
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="got">got</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="have">have</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="should">should</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="must">must</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="at">at</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="in">in</button>
    </div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>I’ve <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="got" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> a headache! &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(A1 lesson · have got)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>You look tired. You <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="should" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> go to bed early. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(A2 lesson · advice, not obligation)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>I take my vitamins <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="at" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> night, after dinner. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(A1 lesson · parts of the day)</span></span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Meet the body</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p>The parts of the body, from head to foot. Say each one aloud with <span class="ex">This is my…</span> for one, or <span class="ex">These are my…</span> for two or more.</p>
  <div class="figure-grid">
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/brain.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">brain</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/eyes.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">eyes</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/ear.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">ear</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/nose.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">nose</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/mouth.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">mouth</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/tooth.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">tooth</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/arm.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">arm</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/hand.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">hand</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/heart-organ.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">heart</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/lungs.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">lungs</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/bone.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">bone</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/leg.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">leg</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/foot.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">foot</span></div>
  </div>

  <h2>At the doctor</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p>The people and things you meet when you are sick. Say each one aloud in a short sentence: <span class="ex">I feel sick. I need to see a doctor.</span></p>
  <div class="figure-grid">
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/sick.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">feel sick</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/doctor.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">doctor</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/stethoscope.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">stethoscope</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/pill.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">medicine</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/syringe.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">shot</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/bandage.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">bandage</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/hospital.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">hospital</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/ambulance.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">ambulance</span></div>
  </div>

  <h2>Notice before the rule</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>Read the talk with the doctor</h3>
    <p><span class="ex">“Good morning. What’s the problem? · I <strong>have a headache</strong> and <strong>a sore throat</strong>, and <strong>my back hurts</strong>. · Do you <strong>have a fever</strong>? · Yes, my temperature is high. · Then <strong>you should rest</strong> today and drink a lot of water. <strong>Take this medicine</strong> twice a day, and you’ll <strong>feel better</strong> soon.”</span></p>
    <ul>
      <li>Look at <span class="ex">I have a headache</span> and <span class="ex">Do you have a fever?</span> Which little verb carries the symptom? Which small word comes before it?</li>
      <li>Now look at <span class="ex">my back hurts</span>. There is no <span class="ex">have</span> here. What does the body part do in this sentence?</li>
      <li>The doctor says <span class="ex">you should rest</span>, not <span class="ex">you should to rest</span>. What comes directly after <span class="ex">should</span>?</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill>
    <h3>Discovery check · read the cue, then choose</h3>
    <p class="choice-hint">Symptom → <b>have + a</b>. Pain → <b>body part + hurts</b>. Advice → <b>should + base verb</b>.</p>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Answer choices">
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="have">have</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="hurts">hurts</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="sore">sore</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="fever">fever</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="should">should</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="feel">feel</button>
    </div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>I <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="have" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> a cough and a cold. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(name the symptom)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>My head <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="hurts" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button>. I need to sit down. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(the body part does the verb)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>I have a <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="sore" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> throat. It hurts when I speak. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(word that goes with throat)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>My temperature is very high. I think I have a <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="fever" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button>. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(high temperature)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span>You <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="should" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> see a doctor about that. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(advice)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">6</span><span>I don’t <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="feel" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> well today. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(how you are, in general)</span></span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>The system: have a symptom, or it hurts</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p>To name a symptom, use <span class="ex">have + a</span>: <span class="ex">I have a headache. I have a fever. I have a cough. I have a cold. I have a sore throat.</span></p>
  <p>To say where the pain is, make the body part the subject and use the verb <span class="ex">hurt</span>: <span class="ex">My back hurts. My tooth hurts.</span> With a plural body part, drop the <span class="ex">-s</span>: <span class="ex">My feet hurt. My eyes hurt.</span></p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>say the symptom <span class="contraction">have + a</span></th><th>say where it hurts <span class="contraction">body part + hurts</span></th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><b>I have a headache.</b></td><td><b>My head hurts.</b></td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>I have a toothache.</b></td><td><b>My tooth hurts.</b></td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>I have a backache.</b></td><td><b>My back hurts.</b></td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>I have a stomachache.</b></td><td><b>My stomach hurts.</b></td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>I have a sore throat.</b></td><td><b>My throat hurts.</b></td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <div class="note">
    <h3>Meaning check</h3>
    <ul>
      <li><span class="ex">Hurt</span> is a verb, so the body part is the subject: <span class="ex">My back hurts</span>, never <span class="ex">My back is hurt</span> for everyday pain. One part takes <span class="ex">hurts</span>; two or more take <span class="ex">hurt</span>: <span class="ex">My feet hurt.</span></li>
      <li><span class="ex">Ache</span> lives inside symptom nouns: <span class="ex">headache, toothache, backache, stomachache</span>. Use them with <span class="ex">have + a</span>: <span class="ex">I have a backache</span> = <span class="ex">My back hurts</span>.</li>
      <li>Say <span class="ex">I have a cold</span> for the illness. <span class="ex">I am cold</span> means you need a sweater, not a doctor.</li>
      <li>You met <span class="ex">should</span> in the modals lesson. It gives advice, softer than <span class="ex">must</span>, and takes the base verb with no <span class="ex">to</span>: <span class="ex">You should rest. You shouldn’t work today.</span></li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <h2>From the first call to feeling better</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p>A doctor’s visit follows the same five steps almost every time. Learn them as chunks, in order:</p>
  <p><span class="ex"><strong>make an appointment</strong> → <strong>see a doctor</strong> → <strong>get a prescription</strong> → <strong>take medicine</strong> → <strong>feel better</strong></span></p>
  <p>In a sentence: <span class="ex">I made an appointment for Monday. I saw the doctor, got a prescription, and took the medicine twice a day. Now I feel better.</span></p>

  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill>
    <h3>Drill 1 · symptom and advice chunks</h3>
    <p class="choice-hint">Chunks to reuse: <b>have + a symptom</b>, <b>body part + hurts / hurt</b>, <b>should + base verb</b>, <b>make an appointment</b>, <b>see a doctor</b>, <b>get a prescription</b>, <b>take medicine</b>.</p>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Answer choices">
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="have">have</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="hurts">hurts</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="hurt">hurt</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="should">should</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="make">make</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="see">see</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="get">get</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="take">take</button>
    </div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>I <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="have" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> a headache and a sore throat. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(name the symptom)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>My back <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="hurts" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> after work. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(one body part · add -s)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>My feet <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="hurt" data-placeholder="choose" data-hint="Feet is plural, so the verb has no -s." data-fix="hurt">choose</button> at the end of the day. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(plural · no -s)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>You <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="should" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> rest today and drink a lot of water. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(advice)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span>First, call the clinic and <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="make" data-placeholder="choose" data-hint="The collocation is make an appointment." data-fix="make">choose</button> an appointment. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(collocation · appointment)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">6</span><span>You should <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="see" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> a doctor about that cough. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(chunk · a doctor)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">7</span><span><button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="get" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> a prescription from the doctor before you leave. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(the doctor gives it to you)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">8</span><span>You should <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="take" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> the medicine twice a day, with food. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(chunk · medicine)</span></span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <div class="practice" data-answer-drill>
    <h3>Drill 2 · type the symptom word</h3>
    <p class="choice-hint">Read the cue in parentheses, then type one word. Say the whole sentence aloud after you check.</p>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>I have a <input class="answer-input" data-answer="headache" aria-label="answer 1" />. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(your head hurts)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>I have a sore <input class="answer-input" data-answer="throat" aria-label="answer 2" />. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(it hurts when you speak or swallow)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>My temperature is very high. I have a <input class="answer-input" data-answer="fever" aria-label="answer 3" />. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(high temperature)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>I have a bad <input class="answer-input" data-answer="cough" aria-label="answer 4" />, so my throat is tired. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(you do it all day when you are sick)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span>My tooth hurts. I have a <input class="answer-input" data-answer="toothache" aria-label="answer 5" data-hint="Join the body part and ache into one word." data-fix="toothache" />. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(one word · body part + ache)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">6</span><span>Rest and take your medicine, and soon you will feel <input class="answer-input" data-answer="better" aria-label="answer 6" />. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(the happy end of the story)</span></span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-answers>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-answers>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Read and choose</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>A message calling in sick</h3>
    <p><span class="ex">“Hi Dana, I’m sorry, but I can’t come to work today. I have a fever and a bad cough, and my whole body aches. I have a doctor’s appointment at 10:30 this morning. I’ll send you an update after I see the doctor. I hope I’ll feel better and be back tomorrow. · Omar”</span></p>
  </div>
  <div class="quiz" data-quiz data-success-message="Good reading. You understood a real message calling in sick to work.">
    <h3>Read, then choose</h3>
    <div class="quiz-list">
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="He is sick.">
        <p class="quiz-question">1. Why can’t Omar come to work today?</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="He is sick.">He is sick.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="He is traveling.">He is traveling.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="He has a meeting.">He has a meeting.</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="10:30">
        <p class="quiz-question">2. What time is his doctor’s appointment?</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="10:30">10:30</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="12:30">12:30</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="3:00">3:00</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="tomorrow">
        <p class="quiz-question">3. When does Omar hope to be back at work?</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="tomorrow">tomorrow</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="today">today</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="next week">next week</button></div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-quiz>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-quiz>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Build the meaning, then the sentence</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>

  <div class="tile-game" data-tile-builder data-answer="i have a sore throat">
    <h3>Drill 3 · build the symptom</h3>
    <p class="tile-target">It hurts when you speak. Build the sentence, then say it to your doctor.</p>
    <div class="tile-bank" data-build-bank>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="throat">throat</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="i">I</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="sore">sore</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="have">have</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="a">a</button>
    </div>
    <div class="build-area" data-build-area data-placeholder="Tap words in order"></div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-build>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-build>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <div class="tile-game" data-tile-builder data-answer="you should make an appointment">
    <h3>Drill 4 · build the advice</h3>
    <p class="tile-target">Your friend has been sick for three days. Give the advice, then say it aloud.</p>
    <div class="tile-bank" data-build-bank>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="appointment">appointment</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="you">You</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="make">make</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="should">should</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="an">an</button>
    </div>
    <div class="build-area" data-build-area data-placeholder="Tap words in order"></div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-build>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-build>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Notice and repair errors</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="is" data-fix="My head hurts." data-why="Hurt is a verb here, so the body part does the action: My head hurts. There is no is.">
    <h3>Drill 5 · the body part does the verb</h3>
    <p>Tap the word that is wrong. Remember how English says where the pain is.</p>
    <div class="spot-options">
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="my">My</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="head">head</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="is">is</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="hurt">hurt.</button>
    </div>
    <p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="to" data-fix="You should rest today." data-why="After should, use the base verb with no to: You should rest.">
    <h3>Drill 6 · advice without to</h3>
    <p>Tap the word that is wrong. Think about what comes after <span class="ex">should</span>.</p>
    <div class="spot-options">
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="you">You</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="should">should</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="to">to</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="rest">rest</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="today">today.</button>
    </div>
    <p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <div class="micro-drill" data-transform>
    <h3>Drill 7 · say it the other way</h3>
    <p>Say the new sentence aloud first, using the pattern in the cue. Reveal only after you answer.</p>
    <div class="transform-list">
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item>
        <p class="transform-cue"><b>1</b> head &nbsp;→&nbsp; say the symptom with <span class="ex">have</span></p>
        <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button>
        <p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>I have a headache.</strong></p>
      </div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item>
        <p class="transform-cue"><b>2</b> throat &nbsp;→&nbsp; say the symptom with <span class="ex">sore</span></p>
        <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button>
        <p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>I have a sore throat.</strong></p>
      </div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item>
        <p class="transform-cue"><b>3</b> I have a backache. &nbsp;→&nbsp; say it with <span class="ex">hurts</span></p>
        <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button>
        <p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>My back hurts.</strong></p>
      </div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item>
        <p class="transform-cue"><b>4</b> My tooth hurts. &nbsp;→&nbsp; say it with <span class="ex">have</span></p>
        <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button>
        <p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>I have a toothache.</strong></p>
      </div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item>
        <p class="transform-cue"><b>5</b> Your coworker has a fever. &nbsp;→&nbsp; give advice with <span class="ex">should</span> + <span class="ex">see a doctor</span></p>
        <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button>
        <p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>You should see a doctor.</strong></p>
      </div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item>
        <p class="transform-cue"><b>6</b> You took the medicine and rested all weekend. &nbsp;→&nbsp; say how you are now with <span class="ex">feel</span></p>
        <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button>
        <p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>I feel better.</strong></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2>Use it in real life</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>At the doctor:</b> Role-play with the teacher. The teacher is the doctor and asks <span class="ex">What’s the problem?</span> Describe at least three symptoms. <span class="ex">I have a sore throat and a fever, and my back hurts.</span></div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Give the advice:</b> Now you are the doctor. The teacher names a problem; answer with <span class="ex">should</span> or <span class="ex">shouldn’t</span>. <span class="ex">You should rest and drink water. You shouldn’t go to the gym this week.</span></div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Interview the teacher:</b> Ask three questions about health habits, then report one answer. <span class="ex">How often do you exercise? Do you sleep well? Do you ever get headaches?</span></div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Your exercise routine:</b> Say what you do for your body and when. <span class="ex">I usually walk to work. I go to the gym twice a week, and I never skip breakfast.</span></div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Call in sick:</b> Leave a polite voice message for your manager: say the problem, the plan, and when you hope to return. <span class="ex">I’m sorry, but I can’t come in today. I have a fever, and I have a doctor’s appointment at ten. I hope I’ll be back tomorrow.</span></div>

  <h2>Reflect</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>Explain the system</h3>
    <p>Complete this aloud: “To name a symptom, I use <strong>have + a</strong>: I have a ______. To say where the pain is, the body part does the verb: My back ______. To give advice, I use ______ and the base verb, with no <strong>to</strong>.”</p>
    <p>Then tell the teacher about the last time you were sick: what did you have, what did you do, and when did you feel better?</p>
  </div>

